    {
      "text": "Just like a plant, it uses photosynthesis. As a result, it is always enveloped in clear air.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its cellular composition is closer to that of a plant than an animal. It uses photosynthesis to produce its energy supply without eating food.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "The younger they are, the more they smell like fresh grass. With age, their fragrance takes on the odor of fallen leaves.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Although it doesn’t like disputes, it will sharpen the leaf on its tail into a blade and fight if it has to protect its friends.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It gets its nutrition from photosynthesis. It lives a quiet life deep in forests where clean rivers flow.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Galarians favor the distinctive aroma that drifts from this Pokémon’s leaves. There’s a popular perfume made using that scent.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon’s tail is blade sharp, with a fantastic cutting edge that can slice right though large trees.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cells similar to those of plants have been found in its fur. Its hard tail can fell a large tree with one stroke, and the tail's sharpness exceeds even that of a sword crafted by a master.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
